.TH SHWETANK 1 "2026-07-30" "shwetank 2026.7.30" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shwetank \- developer, student, builder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shwetank
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shwetank
prints a business card to standard output.
.PP
Builds products end to end, from the Postgres schema to the pixel. Studies at
Scaler School of Technology, Bangalore. Works from a terminal, inside
.BR nvim (1),
on Arch.
.PP
There is no daemon and no configuration file. It prints the card and exits,
which is more than most software manages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit. Versioning is CalVer, because a human is not
semantically versioned and pretending otherwise invites breaking changes.
.TP
.B \-\-hire\-me
Print the short pitch.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Open this page. You are already here.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Declared at runtime:
.BR typescript (1)
as the default dialect,
.BR python (1)
3.13 for anything that involves prying a device open,
.BR node (1)
for APIs and CLIs,
.BR psql (1)
for the parts that have to still be correct next year, and C++ for when speed
is the actual feature.
.PP
Currently installing:
.B rust
(fighting the borrow checker, winning sometimes) and
.BR docker (1).
Neither is claimed as fluent, because the internet can read a commit history.
.PP
Build\-time only:
.BR git (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR nvim (1),
and Arch Linux, btw.
.SH OUTPUT
Selected artifacts, all of which exist and can be verified:
.TP
.B kbrgb
A userspace driver for the Acer ENE KB5130 i2c\-HID keyboard controller, written
after discovering that the vendor's WMI interface accepts every command and
silently does nothing. One Python file, zero dependencies, 29 animated effects.
Available from the AUR and PyPI, so the next person with this laptop does not
have to repeat the reverse\-engineering.
.TP
.B RailRaag
Every train in India, drawn in light: 9,298 trains derived from 183,000
timetable rows, routed over real OpenStreetMap track by Dijkstra across a
612,000\-node graph, rendered in raw WebGL2 at roughly 0.3 ms per frame. No
runtime dependencies, because adding a library felt like cheating.
.TP
.B Claribb.AI
A multi\-agent research workspace with pgvector semantic memory and four agents
(Recall, Explorer, Critique, Connector) running in parallel on every query.
Top 4 at the Ventures Hackathon, built by a team of four.
.TP
.B shellmon
A terminal pet that feeds on your development activity. It is the only
dependency in this list with feelings.
.TP
.B CipherDrop
Zero\-knowledge file transfer: AES\-256\-GCM in the browser, key in the URL
fragment, so the server is structurally incapable of reading what it stores.
.PP
Three packages are published on npm:
.BR shwetank ,
.B shellmon
and
.BR make\-npx\-card .
The first one is this card, but interactive, which is either recursion or a
cry for help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to any value, output is printed without ANSI escapes. Also honoured
automatically when standard output is not a terminal, because a business card
piped into
.BR grep (1)
should not fight back.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The card printed.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown option was given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print the card:
.PP
.RS
.EX
$ shwetank
.EE
.RE
.PP
The same card, over HTTP, because the website content\-negotiates on your user
agent and serves terminals plain text:
.PP
.RS
.EX
$ curl shwetank.is-a.dev
.EE
.RE
.PP
The interactive version, which requires Node:
.PP
.RS
.EX
$ npx shwetank
.EE
.RE
.PP
The website is also a real git remote, served over git's dumb HTTP protocol.
Cloning it gets you a repository with one commit per release and a PKGBUILD:
.PP
.RS
.EX
$ git clone https://shwetank.is-a.dev
.EE
.RE
